{"annotations": [], "blocks": [{"bbox": [36.8503, 62.76988259999996, 287.94511200000005, 136.9846544666667], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 3, "seq": 0, "source": "docling", "text": "these guidelines did not specifically address secondary prophylaxis. In scenarios in which primary prophylaxis is not recommended, that does not preclude that secondary prophylaxis would be appropriate in a similar patient population, and clinicians need to consider each individual patient's clinical situation. An a priori decision was made that antiplatelet therapy (eg, aspirin, clopidogrel) was out of scope for these recommendations."}, {"bbox": [36.8503, 150.98295659999997, 287.9391144, 290.90466846666664], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 3, "seq": 1, "source": "docling", "text": "For most recommendations, there was insufficient evidence for definitive risk stratification of the pediatric subgroups addressed in these guidelines. The risk factors for VTE and bleeding identified for each recommendation are those explicitly discussed in the evidence that informed the guidelines. Although the panel acknowledges the existence of other known VTE risk factors, such as sickle cell disease and nephrotic syndrome, these were not included unless specifically addressed in the supporting evidence for each recommendation. The panel delineated high- and low-risk scenarios based solely on the risk factors explicitly listed in the literature supporting the specific PICO (population/problem, intervention, comparison, and outcome) question, ensuring that the recommendations are grounded in the available evidence."}, {"bbox": [305.85791, 62.81245039999999, 496.6596930000001, 85.11599286666672], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 3, "seq": 2, "source": "docling", "text": "Interpretation of strong and conditional recommendations"}, {"bbox": [305.85791, 91.90977459999999, 556.9169378000001, 133.2428944666667], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 3, "seq": 3, "source": "docling", "text": "The strength of a recommendation is expressed as either strong ('the guideline panel recommends…'), or conditional ('the guideline panel suggests…'), and should be interpreted as described in Figure 1."}, {"bbox": [305.85791, 145.98029739999993, 510.1032358000001, 155.3584248666666], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 3, "seq": 4, "source": "docling", "text": "Interpretation of good practice statements"}, {"bbox": [305.85791, 162.15275559999998, 556.9312264479998, 225.3699694666667], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 3, "seq": 5, "source": "docling", "text": "As described by the GRADE guidance group, good practice statements endorse interventions or practices that the panel agreed have unequivocal net benefit yet may not be widely recognized or used. 24 Good practice statements in these guidelines are not based on a systematic review of available evidence. Nevertheless, they may be interpreted as strong recommendations."}, {"bbox": [305.85791, 239.12739239999996, 395.3021328000002, 248.50551986666665], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 3, "seq": 6, "source": "docling", "text": "Recommendations"}, {"bbox": [305.85791, 255.76175880000005, 438.1766483999999, 264.20194173333334], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 3, "seq": 7, "source": "docling", "text": "Pediatric patients with cancer"}, {"bbox": [305.85791, 271.73991459999996, 556.9228184000001, 291.13354946666664], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 3, "seq": 8, "source": "docling", "text": "RECOMMENDATION 1. In pediatric patients with leukemia/lymphoblastic lymphoma, the ASH/International Society on Thrombosis"}, {"bbox": [182.041, 710.8814688, 411.71004750000003, 717.4460450666667], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "caption", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 3, "seq": 9, "source": "docling", "text": "Figure 1. Interpretation of strong and conditional recommendations."}], "checksum": "677755064190d82094f7b5e1e131d741b34697c686b19f852850a35947e5c3f8", "content_present": true, "doc_id": "d-97b717427b6bf503", "docling_version": "2.118.0", "engine_version": "2.118.0", "errors": [], "images": [], "page_index": 2, "page_sizes": {"3": [593.9719848632812, 782.9860229492188]}, "route": "docling", "schema_version": "v0.1.0", "source_hash": "97b717427b6bf503d2817d27c02c788bde996058c4ef8ebaee3678ae31782ea1", "status": "ok", "tables": [{"bbox": [84.35116982887584, 312.65021113047226, 509.57057021185756, 700.1053613351651], "body_bottom": 680.267057, "caption": "Figure 1. Interpretation of strong and conditional recommendations.", "cell_bboxes": [[null, [147.104782, 354.01938399999995, 299.489801, 361.08938399999994], [334.214783, 354.01938399999995, 374.06228300000004, 361.08938399999994], [420.149796, 354.01938399999995, 488.5947960000001, 361.08938399999994], null], [null, [182.57230399999997, 428.449376, 267.112304, 444.51937599999997], [356.57228100000003, 428.449376, 464.6997810000001, 444.51937599999997], [356.57228100000003, 428.449376, 464.6997810000001, 444.51937599999997], null], [[103.162281, 454.11436999999995, 324.022284, 479.23689], [103.162281, 454.11436999999995, 324.022284, 479.23689], [310.37980699999997, 454.16688999999997, 516.8023070000003, 488.23689], [310.37980699999997, 454.16688999999997, 516.8023070000003, 488.23689], null], [[100.589779, 505.894368, 140.594779, 512.9643679999999], [145.739777, 505.946889, 316.387277, 549.0169040000001], [145.739777, 505.94690399999996, 515.86